<h2 id="ha-ctrl-014-acceptance">Acceptance and evidence</h2>

1. Test Home, Away, a named zone, Unknown, Unavailable and a stale retained report. A missing reading must never look like Away.
2. Compare a person with no login, a user with no tracked person and a linked pair. Neither presence nor sign-in may stand for the other.
3. Use conflicting or delayed tracker reports in a made-up setup. Keep the native result, and mark the uncertainty without guessing a cause.
4. Review private and shared displays, notification previews and public screenshots. Check names, coordinates, avatars, timestamps, keyboard alternatives and the stated limit on who may see them.

Record the integration and frontend versions, the browser, the fixture or device, the input state, the expected and observed results and where the evidence is kept, using [Native task accessibility and evidence](native-task-accessibility.html). Documentation checks and a source review do not verify a live device. Record any native limitation you cannot resolve.

